<article class="env-lemma" id="0B77">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0B77">Lemma <span data-tag="0B77">42.34.3</span>.</a> Let $(S, \delta )$ be as in Situation <a href="/tag/02QL" data-tag="02QL">42.7.1</a>. Let $X$ be locally of finite type over $S$. Let $\mathcal{L}$ be an invertible $\mathcal{O}_ X$-module. Then the rule that to $f : X' \to X$ assigns $c_1(f^*\mathcal{L}) \cap - : \mathop{\mathrm{CH}}\nolimits _ k(X') \to \mathop{\mathrm{CH}}\nolimits _{k - 1}(X')$ is a bivariant class of degree $1$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This follows from Lemmas <a href="/tag/02TI" data-tag="02TI">42.28.2</a>, <a href="/tag/02SU" data-tag="02SU">42.26.4</a>, <a href="/tag/02SS" data-tag="02SS">42.26.2</a>, and <a href="/tag/0B72" data-tag="0B72">42.30.4</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>